A||||10||grgoyl86||Duke Tech Day!||||1||
Z||000000||grgoyl86||12-22-2001||10:18 PM||||Wanna learn a few tricks to make that 2.5 litre Iron Duke engine perform at it's best? Maybe even eek a little extra oomph out of it? <P>Join us for Duke Tech Day. We'll talk about tune-up tips, and some after-market add-ons, like intake manifolds, throttle bodies, carbs, headers, and so on.<P>There are a lot of performance parts out there for the Duke that most people don't know exist because of what they've heard. They think it's slow so no one would modify it. There are a lot of reasons to modify a Duke and the best is that it is REALLY easy to work on, and simple to modify. I have three different performance intakes and there are at least that many more I don't have. These parts are also pretty easy to find.<P>The date for the Duke hop-up tech day is Dec. 29th. It will be held at the Kline's place near Allentown, PA, and it will be inside. They will have Chili for everyone but would appreciate some drinks and chips and snacks. They may need a few chairs, so you might want to bring your folding chairs.<P>For directions and more information, check out <A HREF="http://www.fieropride.com/duke_tech_day.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieropride.com/duke_tech_day.htm</A> <P>Please let us know if you are coming. Send a email to RACINCOUPLE@webtv.net and let'em know!||||reg||1
Z||000001||grgoyl86||12-22-2001||10:29 PM||||The weather report looks promising (except cold).<BR>I'll be heading up from York, PA, taking I83 to I81 to I78. Anyone along that route want to meet up and travel together?<P>Bob||||reg||1
